    "content": "{\n  \"search_id\": \"search_ff83e6feaa6358f393bac2120a4f4a58\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://science.uptrusthq.com/paper/e7dcfbfa0f3150ec21386601030ab456e6b72a2f\",\n      \"title\": \"Kriging metamodeling in simulation: A review — Sci-Trust\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"developing a non-dynamic mapping (regression) of the complex model inputs into the outputs, namely objective functions and/or constraints (Bieker et al., 2007; Blanning, 1975; Broad et al., 2005; Broad et al., 2010; Gorissen et al., 2010; Keating et al., 2010; Kleijnen, 2009; Laloy et al., 2013; Que\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/1642420\",\n      \"title\": \"Efficient Surrogate Model Development: Impact of Sample ...\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2020-07-20\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Sobol and Halton sequences are both quasi-random low-discrepancy sequences, which seek to distribute samples uniformly across the input space. These methods were selected as they are shown to sample input space uniformly with limited sample sizes for functions up to ten dimensions (Dife and Diwekar, 2016).\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://science.uptrusthq.com/paper/8c66677f01ac652c8a86b6e5523ff96850e53bbc\",\n      \"title\": \"Optimization and uncertainty assessment of strongly nonlinear… — Sci-Trust\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Efficient posterior exploration of a high‐dimensional groundwater model from two‐stage Markov chain Monte Carlo simulation and polynomial chaos expansion\\nEric Laloy , B. Rogiers , Jasper A. Vrugt , Dirk Mallants , Diederik Jacques · 2013\\n…are not very well resolved [e.g., Carrera and Neuman, 1986a, 1986b; Kitanidis, 1986, 1997; Carrera et al., 2005; Cooley and Christensen, 2006; Hernandez et al., 2006; Tonkin and Doherty, 2009; Keating et al., 2010; Troldborg et al., 2010; Nowak et al., 2010; Zeng and Zhang, 2010, and many others].\\nFor parameter optimization, Bayesian‐based methods have gained considerable attention from the environmental modeling community because they provide a powerful tool from which inferences can be drawn (Clark & Gelfand, 2006; Huisman et al., 2010; Keating et al., 2010; Zhu et al., 2014).\\nOne of the most popular and robust sampling techniques is the Markov Chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) method [Marshall et al., 2005; Gamerman and Lopes, 2006; Vrugt et al., 2008, 2009; Keating et al., 2010; Liu et al., 2010].\\nNeutral Referenced without endorsement\\n5\\nReview of surrogate modeling in water resources\\nSaman Razavi , Bryan Tolson , Donald H.\\nBurn · 2012\\nModern simulation models tend to be computationally intensive as they rigorously represent detailed scientific knowledge about the real-world systems [Keating et al., 2010; Mugunthan et al., 2005; Zhang et al., 2009].\\nMarkov chain Monte Carlo simulation using the DREAM software package: Theory, concepts, and MATLAB implementation\\nJasper A. Vrugt · Environmental Modelling & Software 2016\\n, 2011), hydrologeology (Keating et al., 2010; Laloy et al., 2013; Malama et al., 2013), hydrology (Vrugt et al.\\nGlobal sensitivity analysis in hydrological modeling: Review of concepts, methods, theoretical framework, and applications\\nXiaomeng Song , Jianyun Zhang , Che-sheng Zhan , Yunqing Xuan , Ming Ye , Chonggang Xu · 2015\\nModel calibration or parameter optimization is challenging for complex models due to the uncertainty of a large number of parameters (Fienen et al., 2009; Foglia et al., 2009; Keating et al., 2010; Ye et al., 2014).\\nPhysically based modeling in catchment hydrology at 50: Survey and outlook\\nClaudio Paniconi , Mario Putti · 2015\\nFor PDE-based numerical models the main challenges to robust calibration and estimation regard computational cost, nonunique solutions (ill-posedness), and multiple possible objectives and variables [e.g., Anderman and Hill, 1999; Keating et al., 2010].\\nNumerical assessment of metamodelling strategies in computationally intensive optimization\\nSaman Razavi , Bryan Tolson , Donald H. Burn · 2012\\nA single run of such models can be prohibitively long, in the order of minutes to days (Keating et al., 2010; Razavi et al., 2010; Wang and Shan, 2007; Zhang et al., 2009); while in many optimization-based engineering practices, such as design\\nSci-Trust\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"warnings\": null,\n  \"metadata\": null,\n  \"session_id\": \"ses_ea95fb574ffeu0UL1viRR0U87M\"\n}"
