    "content": "{\n  \"search_id\": \"search_f9a22f618c6b0d4b3987e326bb31270b\",\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://gmd.copernicus.org/preprints/gmd-2018-272/gmd-2018-272-AR3.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"Bold black font: Topical editor and reviewer comments Black font: Author response Topical Editor Decision: Publish subject to technical corrections\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"the soil respiration model parameters using the MT-DREAM(ZS) code (Laloy and Vrugt, 2012). 319\\nMT-DREAM(ZS) implements a Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) algorithm by running 320\\nmultiple Markov chains in parallel with adaptive proposal distribution, multiple-try sampling, and 321\\nsampling from an archive of past states.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1029/2011wr010608\",\n      \"title\": \"High‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models ...\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"High‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models ...\\nby E Laloy · 2012 · Cited by 663 — Here we present our latest algorithmic developments and introduce MT-DREAM(ZS), which combines the strengths of multiple-try sampling, snooker\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1029/2011wr010608\",\n      \"title\": \"High‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models ...\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"High‐dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models ...\\nby E Laloy · 2012 · Cited by 663 — In this paper, we present a general framework for efficient inversion of highly parameterized models. This method, entitled MT-DREAM(ZS),\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://www.osti.gov/servlets/purl/2417772\",\n      \"title\": \"Quantifying subsurface parameter and transport uncertainty using surrogate modelling and environmental tracers\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2022-11-01\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Thiros, Department of Geosciences, University of Montana, Missoula, MT 59812, USA. Email: nicholas.thiros@umontana.edu\\nFunding information Department of Energy NEUP, Grant/Award Number: NU-18-MT-UM-040102-04; National Science Foundation National Research Traineeship, Grant/Award Number: DGE-1633831\\nAbstract\\noriginal physics-based model (Asher et al., 2015; Razavi et al., 2012).\\nFor instance, Laloy and Jacques (2019) and Fienen et al. (2018) com-\\npare the ability of multiple surrogate models to emulate physics-based\\nreactive transport models at the column scale and groundwater flow\\nat regional scale, respectively. Recent studies extend the use of\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2015WR017912\",\n      \"title\": \"A Bayesian approach to improved calibration and prediction of groundwater models with structural error - Xu - 2015 - Water Resources Research - Wiley Online Library\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2015-11-01\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"The presented framework allows explicit treatment of model structural error, while previous applications of Bayesian approaches in the groundwater modeling literature concentrated on parameter uncertainty [ Fienen et al ., 2009 ; Keating et al ., 2010 ; Laloy et al ., 2013 ].\\nIn this study, we use DREAM-ZS (Differential Evolution Adaptive Metropolis algorithm) [ Schoups and Vrugt , 2010 ].\\nOnce sufficient samples urn:x-wiley:00431397:media:wrcr21790:wrcr21790-math-0078 are generated using MCMC, Bayesian inference of prediction uncertainty can be carried out.\\nThe prior distributions of these hyperparameters are further discussed in Appendix Appendix A .\\nThe DREAM-ZS runtime settings were configured following the recommendations in Vrugt et al . [ 2008 ]. The Bayesian calibration and prediction processes were carried out following the procedures outlined in section 2.3.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://bg.copernicus.org/preprints/bg-2017-41/bg-2017-41-SC2-supplement.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"Microsoft Word - Reponse_SC1.docx\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"On the other hand, Laloy and Vrugt (2012) demonstrated that DREAM can successfully sample the 25-dimensional, three-modal Gaussian function with the two neighboring modes having a separation of 10 units.\\nLaloy, E., and J.A. Vrugt: High-dimensional posterior exploration of hudrologic models using multiply-try DREAM(zs) and high-performance computing, Water resour. Res., 48, W01526, 2012.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://openalex.org/works/W2133944044\",\n      \"title\": \"Efficient posterior exploration of a high‐dimensional groundwater model from two‐stage Markov chain Monte Carlo simulation and polynomial chaos expansion\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"description: 2013 article in Water Resources Research by Laloy, Rogiers, Vrugt and 2 others; 264 citations; open access title: Efficient posterior exploration of a high‐dimensional groundwater model from two‐stage Markov chain Monte Carlo simulation and polynomial chaos expansion image: https://openalex.org/brand-assets/openalex-mark-square.png\\nAuthors: Eric Laloy, Bart Rogiers, Jasper A. Vrugt, Dirk Mallants, Diederik Jacques\\nInstitutions: Belgian Nuclear Research Centre, KU Leuven, University of California, Irvine, University of Amsterdam, Commonwealth Scientific and Industrial Research Organisation, CSIRO Land and Water\\nshow all 6\\nLanguage: English\\nLaloy\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://openalex.org/authors/A5042170410\\\",\\\"sameAs\\\":[\\\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4788-3272\\\"],\\\"affiliation\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Organization\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Belgian Nuclear Research\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://gmd.copernicus.org/preprints/gmd-2018-272/gmd-2018-272-AC2.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"Interactive comment on “Bayesian Inference and Predictive Performance of Soil Respiration Models in the Presence of Model Discrepancy” by Ahmed\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2019-03-14\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"We clarified this in the revised manuscript “the posterior distributions of the data model parameters are jointly estimated with the soil respiration model parameters using the MT-DREAM(ZS) code (Laloy and Vrugt, 2012).” In addition, a summary of the data model parameters is presented in the sup- plementary materials as we clarified in a previous\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/jaspervrugt/DREAM-Suite\",\n      \"title\": \"GitHub - jaspervrugt/DREAM-Suite: DiffeRential Evolution Adaptive Metropolis algorithm: MATLAB and Python Toolbox · GitHub\",\n      \"publish_date\": null,\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"$\\\\tilde{\\\\textbf{y}}$ . Unfortunately, for complex system models the posterior distribution is often high dimensional and analytically intractable, and sampling methods are required to approximate the target. DREAM-Suite is a MATLAB and Python toolbox of the DiffeRential Evolution Adaptive Metropolis (DREAM) algorithm of Vrugt et al.\\n2008a, 2009a and implements in one package the DREAM$ {(LOA)}$ (Vrugt and Beven, 2018), DREAM$ {(ABC)}$ (Sadegh and Vrugt, 2014), DREAM$ {(BMA)}$ (Vrugt et al., 2008b), DREAM$ {(D)}$ (Vrugt and ter Braak, 2011), DREAM$ {(ZS)}$, MTDREAM$ {(ZS)}$ (Laloy and Vrugt, 2012) and DREAM$_{(KZS)}$ (Zhang et al., 2020) algorithms.\\n4335–4345, https://doi.org/10.1002/wrcr.20354\\n9. Laloy, E., and J.A. Vrugt (2012), High-dimensional posterior exploration of hydrologic models using multiple-try DREAM_(ZS) and high-performance computing, Water Resources Research , 48, W01526, https://doi.org/10.1029/2011WR010608\\n10. Vrugt, J.A., and C.J.F.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"url\": \"https://gmd.copernicus.org/preprints/gmd-2018-272/gmd-2018-272-AC2-print.pdf\",\n      \"title\": \"“Bayesian Inference and Interactive comment on Predictive Performance of Soil Respiration Models in the Presence of Model Discrepancy” by Ahmed\",\n      \"publish_date\": \"2019-03-14\",\n      \"excerpts\": [\n        \"Response: The parameters of the data model are jointly estimated with the parameters of the soil respiration model using MCMC.\\nWe clarified this in the revised manuscript “the posterior distributions of the data model parameters are jointly estimated with the soil respiration model parameters using the MT-DREAM(ZS) code (Laloy and Vrugt, 2012).” In addition, a summary of the data model parameters is presented in the sup- plementary materials as we clarified in a previous\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"warnings\": null,\n  \"metadata\": null,\n  \"session_id\": \"ses_ea95fb574ffeu0UL1viRR0U87M\"\n}"
